                  "targets": {
                    "value": "1 creature"
                  },
                  "description": {
                    "value": "The target appears to be a gruesome and terrifying creature.\n\nThe effect is unique to each observer, so a human viewing the target might see a demon with bloody fangs, but a demon observing the target might see a glowing angelic visage.\n\nWhen any creature attempts a hostile action against the target, the creature must attempt a Will save. It is then temporarily immune until the end of its next turn.\n\n- **Success:** The creature is unaffected.\n- **Failure:** The creature becomes frightened 2 before using its action.\n- **Critical Failure:** The creature becomes frightened 2, and its action fails and is wasted."
                  },
                  "higher_level_description": {
                    "value": "Heightened (8th): You can target up to 5 creatures. If a creature uses a hostile action or reaction that affects multiple targets simultaneously, it needs to attempt only one save against mask of terror."
                  },
